 HISTORY                                                          4003 1451
 -------                                                          4003 1451
 The inelastic thermal scattering law data for FLiBe was          4003 1451
 developed by the Low Energy Interaction Physics (LEIP) group at  4003 1451
 North Carolina State University (USA) using molecular dynamics   4003 1451
 methods [1,2]. This material is a liquid salt mixture, such that 4003 1451
 the diffusive contribution to the TSL is expected to be          4003 1451
 consequential. The FLASSH code was used with a Schofield         4003 1451
 diffusion model to produce File 7 for Li in FLiBe [3]. Please see4003 1451
 the README for additional information.                           4003 1451
                                                                  4003 1451
